From 7b5f664caaab759757528c5d3a864d0e40eefe3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shreyasajj <shreyas.github@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:57:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] audio/out: add --audio-spdif-pause-bursts

With spdif passthrough, silence (paused with --audio-stream-silence,
underruns, padding) is written as zero bytes, which is not a valid
IEC 61937 stream.

Add an option to write IEC 61937 pause bursts instead: Pa, Pb,
Pc (data type 3), Pd (32 bits) and a gap length, zero padded up to the
repetition period. The period is 4 frames for formats sent at 192 kHz
(E-AC-3, TrueHD, DTS-HD) and 3 frames otherwise, the same values Kodi
uses. The burst phase is kept across calls so the spacing stays even
across buffer boundaries.

Tested with ao=pcm only: the output while paused with
--audio-stream-silence is pause bursts at the expected spacing, and data
bursts are unchanged during playback. Not tested with a receiver.
---
